# Runes and components

### Svelte 5, read through the reader's cards

Tutors Ladder, Reader (rung 4), talk 2

---

## A component is a file

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import Icon from "../../ui-primitives/Icon.svelte";
  let { cardDetails }: { cardDetails: CardDetails } = $props();
  const external = $derived(cardDetails.route?.startsWith("http") ?? false);
</script>

<article class="card" data-lo-type={cardDetails.type}>
  ...
</article>

<style>
  .card { border-block-width: 6px; ... }
</style>
```

Script, markup and styles in one `.svelte` file. Styles are scoped to the component.
`apps/reader/src/lib/ui-components/layout/Card.svelte`

---

## Runes: the four you need here

| Rune | Says | In the reader |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `$props()` | what the parent passes in | every component |
| `$state(x)` | a value that re-renders what reads it | `courseId` on the home page, the shared `rune` |
| `$derived(expr)` | a value computed from others, kept up to date | `Composite`'s `arrange(composite)`, `Lab`'s step |
| `$effect(fn)` | run code after the DOM updates | none here; upstream's root layout sets `<html lang>` with one |

Runes are compiler keywords, not imports. They work in `.svelte` files and in `.svelte.ts` files.

---

## `$state` and binding

`apps/reader/src/routes/+page.svelte`

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  let courseId = $state("ladder-sample-course");
</script>

<label>Course id <input bind:value={courseId} /></label>
<a href={`/course/${courseId}`}>Open the course</a>
```

Type in the box: `courseId` changes, and the link's `href` follows. No event handlers, no setState.

---

## `$derived`, even when destructured

`apps/reader/src/lib/ui-components/structure/Composite.svelte`

```svelte
let { composite }: { composite: Course | Topic } = $props();
const { units, sides, standardLos } = $derived(arrange(composite));
```

When the route changes from one topic to another, SvelteKit reuses the component with a new
`composite`. Plain `const` would keep the first topic's cards; `$derived` recomputes.

`arrange` is plain TypeScript in `lib/course/lo-tree.ts`, tested with `node --test`.

---

## Shared state: a rune behind `.value`

`apps/reader/src/lib/runes/index.svelte.ts`

```ts
export const rune = <T>(initialValue: T) => {
  let value = $state(initialValue);
  return {
    get value() { return value; },
    set value(next: T) { value = next; },
  };
};
export const currentCourse = rune<CourseTree | null>(null);
```

A load sets `currentCourse.value`; `TutorsShell` and `SecondaryNavigator` read it and re-render.
Upstream: `packages/svelte/runes/src/index.svelte.ts`, the same `rune` (created lazily there).

---

## Snippets replace slots

`apps/reader/src/lib/ui-navigators/TutorsShell.svelte`

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import type { Snippet } from "svelte";
  let { children }: { children: Snippet } = $props();
</script>

<a class="skip" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
<header>...</header>
<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
  {@render children()}
</main>
```

What a layout or parent puts between the tags arrives as `children`, a snippet, drawn with `{@render}`.

---

## Cards, mirrored

| Reader (`src/lib/ui-components/`) | Upstream (`packages/svelte/ui-components/src/learning-objects/`) |
| --- | --- |
| `layout/Card.svelte` | `layout/Card.svelte`: `cardDetails` = route, title, type, summary (+ img, icon, video) |
| `layout/Cards.svelte` | `layout/Cards.svelte`: one `Card` per visible learning object |
| `layout/Units.svelte` | `layout/Units.svelte`: each unit a box with a heading and its cards |
| `structure/Composite.svelte` | `structure/Composite.svelte`: one component for course and topic, sides in a column |
| `content/Note.svelte` | `content/Note.svelte` |
| `content/lab/Lab.svelte` | `content/lab/Lab.svelte`: steps, a pager, arrow keys |

Upstream's are bigger: locks, themes, images, video. The shape is the same.

---

## Inside one card

```svelte
<article class="card" data-lo-type={cardDetails.type} style:--accent={loTypeColour[cardDetails.type]}>
  <svelte:element this={cardDetails.route ? "a" : "div"} class="link" href={cardDetails.route} ...>
    <h3>{cardDetails.title}</h3>
    <Icon type={cardDetails.type} />
    <span class="visually-hidden">{cardDetails.type}</span>
  </svelte:element>
  {#if cardDetails.summary}<p>{cardDetails.summary}</p>{/if}
</article>
```

- `data-lo-type` and the hidden type text: upstream's guided tour and screen readers both need the kind.
- `a.link::after { inset: 0 }` makes the whole card clickable, as upstream's `.resource-link::after`.
- An archive has no route here, so its card is a `div`, not a broken link.

---

## Escaping by default

- `{cardDetails.summary}` is escaped by Svelte. Course text never becomes markup.
- `{@html ...}` is not. The reader has one, in `ui-primitives/Markdown.svelte`:

```svelte
const html = $derived(renderMarkdown(markdown).value);
...
<div class="prose">{@html html}</div>
```

`renderMarkdown` comes from `@ladder/lite` (rung 2) and escapes every character before adding tags.
The Raw HTML rule fails on `{@html` anywhere else. Upstream passes author HTML through `sanitizeHtml`
(`packages/svelte/ui-primitives/src/utils/sanitize.ts`); that is rung 6.

---

## Unrepresentable: a colour per kind

`apps/reader/src/lib/ui-primitives/lo-colours.ts`

```ts
export const loTypeColour: Record<LoType, string> = {
  course: "#1d4ed8", topic: "#0f766e", unit: "#4b5563", side: "#4b5563",
  talk: "#b45309", note: "#7c3aed", lab: "#be123c", web: "#0369a1", archive: "#57534e",
};
```

Add a kind to `@ladder/model` and `svelte-check` fails here until it has a colour (L5).
Upstream: `loTypeColour` in `packages/svelte/themes/src/styles/lo-colours.ts`.

---

## The lab: derived step, keyboard path

```svelte
let { liveLab }: { liveLab: LiveLab } = $props();
const { lab, step, index, previous, next } = $derived(liveLab);

function navigateStep(event: KeyboardEvent) {
  ...
  const to = event.key === "ArrowRight" ? next : event.key === "ArrowLeft" ? previous : undefined;
  if (to) { event.preventDefault(); void goto(to.route); }
}
</script>
<svelte:window onkeydown={navigateStep} />
```

`liveLab` (plain data from `lib/course/live-lab.ts`) mirrors upstream's `LiveLab` class:
`setActivePage`, `nextStep`, `prevStep`. Events are attributes in Svelte 5: `onkeydown`, not `on:keydown`.

---

## What to take away

- A component is a file; `$props` in, markup out, scoped styles.
- `$state` for values that change, `$derived` for values computed from them, `.value` runes to share.
- Snippets and `{@render}` for what a parent passes in.
- Escaping is the default; one primitive owns `{@html}`.
- Keep logic in plain TypeScript (`lib/course`) so `node --test` can check it.
